{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator decision (2026-08-16): accept and document the bounded stale-reclaim TOCTOU window. Keep the current advisory-file mechanism; do not add flock or atomic create-and-rename in this ticket. The queue claim remains the correctness boundary, so the residual risk is limited to redundant drain work. Implementation should add a precise code comment documenting that tradeoff and complete the three already-scoped vocabulary/test gaps without changing runtime locking behavior."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786907213171392001,"uuid":"e2858575-5de5-4de4-b060-72f5db62a60e"}